/*****************************************************************************
    decode -- THE RUNNER. Serves a decode line from incant/decoder.

        <binary> incant/decode

    THE USAGE SHAPE, which is the point (docs/decoder.md section 2). A dispatch
    headed for Tony's signature opens with a decode line covering its shorthand
    (WT14). That line is served here: EDIT THE DECODE LINE at the foot and run.

        decodE(H4 H7 blastRadius);

    One call, N names. The verb and the corpus both live in incant/decoder; this
    file is nothing but the invocation, so a decode line is a one-line edit and
    never a copy of the machinery.

    ⚠ `print :;` FOR A BLANK LINE, NEVER `print "":;` -- an empty string literal
    has no data and prints as the string `quoteBody` (bear-trap #26's family).
    Measured 2026-08-09, on the first run of this file.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (H2), single stop().
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);
include(decoder);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities Decoder list;

/*  ---- THE DECODE LINE -- edit this and run --------------------------- */
print "=== decode ===":;
decodE(H4 H7 blastRadius);

print :;
print "=== full corpus ===":;
decodeAll();

print :;
print "DECODE SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
